{
  "abstract": "The six-equation intersection underlying the Croatian olive construction has components beyond its known rational entry curve. We exhibit an explicit geometrically irreducible component whose normalization has genus four, together with seven rational entry functions and a rational inverse. Exact identities establish all six native equations, generic nonzero and distinct entries, and a full-rank native Jacobian at a good finite-field specialization. The regularity identities give twenty literal square roots after adjoining $\\sqrt{1+ab}$; exact norm valuations prove that $1+ab$ and the remaining radicand $1+ec$ represent independent squareclasses. We also give a smooth quadric-cubic model with good reduction at $3$. Its point counts over the first four extensions of $\\mathbb F_3$ are $7,19,34,79$, yielding an irreducible degree-eight Frobenius polynomial. Thus the component's Jacobian is simple over $\\mathbb Q$, excluding every smaller positive-genus quotient defined over $\\mathbb Q$. A local normalization audit resolves the known small-height fibres and all rational branches at plane infinity, with no ordinary return. Small standalone exact-arithmetic certificates reproduce the construction and arithmetic. No ordinary rational point, new almost septuple, septuple, or global rational-point determination is claimed.",
